codex
- [RESOLVED] Joined HEVC with more than one sample entry plays corrupted — fixed with in-band HEVC parameter sets.
  Multi-config HEVC entries are rewritten to `hev1` and the first sample after each config switch gets the new parameter sets prefixed in-band (`lib/utils/mp4_remux.dart:357-375`, `:871-894`). That directly addresses the `hevc_mp4toannexb`/MediaCodec path issue.

- [RESOLVED] Segment re-download deletes the only copy and still completes — preserves data and avoids completion on damaged failure.
  Non-short corrupt segments now download to `<seg>.redl` and swap only after success, while short segments resume in place (`lib/services/download/download_service.dart:848-880`). Merge damage now returns `damaged: true`, and `_completeDownload` stops before `isCompleted = true` (`:597-617`).

- [RESOLVED] Repair download fights the normal download manager slot — repair managers are isolated.
  Repair downloads are tracked in `_repairManagers` instead of `_downloadManager`, so starting another queued item no longer cancels or steals the merge repair slot (`lib/services/download/download_service.dart:842-870`). Deletion cancels the repair manager by cid (`:1166-1169`).

- [RESOLVED] Deleting the export still wipes downloads in a shared folder — shared folders are pruned selectively.
  `_deleteMerged` now detects child entry folders and deletes only non-download export files when an old export folder also contains internal downloads (`lib/services/download/download_service.dart:999-1016`).

- [RESOLVED] Moving an old export aside fails silently when a file is open — no unhandled async failure.
  The rename is wrapped in `try/catch`, so Windows locked-file failures no longer abort `_createDownload` (`lib/services/download/download_service.dart:291-310`). The download proceeds and relies on the existing deletion guards.

- [RESOLVED] `_isForeignFolder` treats OS clutter as foreign — clutter is ignored.
  The foreign-folder check now excludes dotfiles plus `desktop.ini`, `thumbs.db`, and `ehthumbs.db` (`lib/services/download/download_service.dart:1069-1083`).

- [RESOLVED] `checkSegment` misses some damage and can throw — strict checks cover both probes.
  Strict FLV parsing now treats leftover bytes after the last whole tag as damage, and MP4 segment checking catches `RangeError` as damage (`lib/utils/flv_demux.dart:63-67`, `lib/utils/mp4_remux.dart:99-106`).

- [RESOLVED] If the fd cannot be opened, the player still ends up loaded — now errors cleanly.
  `openFd` failure throws so `setDataSource` can enter the error path, and a detached fd is explicitly closed if `player.open` throws before mpv takes ownership (`lib/plugin/pl_player/controller.dart:809-849`).

- [RESOLVED] Picker pending result can be lost — pending state is engine-scoped.
  `pendingPick`, the executor, and the main handler now live in the companion object, matching the cached FlutterEngine lifetime (`android/app/src/main/kotlin/com/example/piliplus/MainActivity.kt:252-265`). `onDestroy` completes and clears only when the activity is finishing (`:283-290`).

- [RESOLVED] Persisted grants are never used — persistent grants were removed.
  The picker no longer requests or stores persistable URI permission, and the code documents that the transient session grant is enough because URI reopen state is not saved (`android/app/src/main/kotlin/com/example/piliplus/MainActivity.kt:117-152`).

- [RESOLVED] Side-file cache is wiped on every open and copies are not atomic — cache lifetime and copies are safer.
  Open video pages retain their mirror folders until `LocalPlayer.release`, and cleanup skips mirrors still in use (`lib/services/local_player.dart:145-183`). Side-file copies now write `.part` first and provider display names are sanitized before being used as cache paths (`android/app/src/main/kotlin/com/example/piliplus/MainActivity.kt:226-247`, `lib/services/local_documents.dart:29-42`).

- [RESOLVED] HEVC tracks are written with width/height 0 — dimensions are parsed from SPS.
  HEVC dimensions now come from the first SPS in `hvcC`, including conformance-window cropping, instead of forcing `(0, 0)` (`lib/utils/flv_demux.dart:340-414`).

- [RESOLVED] Picker `video/*` filter may hide `.mkv` — picker widened and Dart validates.
  Android now uses `*/*` with explicit video-ish MIME hints including Matroska/FLV/octet-stream, then rejects non-video selections in Dart (`MainActivity.kt:45-59`, `lib/services/local_player.dart:72-78`).

- [RESOLVED] Two merges can pick the same export folder — folder is claimed before the first await.
  `_mergeFolders.add(folder.path)` now happens before creating or cleaning the folder, closing the race between overlapping merges with the same title (`lib/services/download/download_service.dart:1127-1142`).

- [PARTIAL] 推荐 change — feed requests bind correctly, but dislike/cancel still short-circuit when the recommend role is anonymous.
  `LoginPolicy.bind` now keeps only `recommendListApp`, `recommendListWeb`, `feedDislike`, and `feedDislikeCancel` for the recommend role in login mode, while other home tabs are still anonymized (`lib/utils/accounts/login_policy.dart:68-124`). However `VideoHttp.feedDislike` and `feedDislikeCancel` return before the request whenever the recommend role has no access key, so the “anonymous if that role is anonymous” route is not honored for those two actions.

- [P2] Feed dislike still cannot use an anonymous recommend role — lib/http/video.dart:479-493
  `LoginPolicy` can now bind `feedDislike`/`feedDislikeCancel` to the recommend role, including `AnonymousAccount`, but both call sites reject locally when `Accounts.get(AccountType.recommend).accessKey` is empty. Remove or revise that precheck so the request actually follows the selected role, or explicitly disable the UI for anonymous recommend.

TOTAL: ROUND-NEEDS-FIX
